  "body": "## What changed\n\n- Add `assets/machines/makera-z1-pro.mch`. It is a copy of `makera-z1.mch` with two changes:\n  - the model is \"Makera Z1 Pro\";\n  - the X/Y/Z `max_normal_speed` and `max_rapid_speed` are 2000 mm/min (the Z1 has 1200).\n\n  The envelope (200 x 200 x 100 mm), the spindle (150 W, 13000 rpm) and the Air M7 coolant are the same as the Z1. The file names the shared \"Makera Carvera\" post.\n- Register the machine in `crates/app/src/posting_files.rs` (the built-in list and the embedded asset table).\n- Add \"Makera Z1 Pro\" to the built-in machine list test in `crates/app/tests/machine.rs`.\n- Extend `crates/app/tests/makera_z1.rs` to the two models through one `MODELS` table. The tests do not make a new test binary.\n- Add the decision record `docs/decisions/4434-makera-z1-pro.md`.\n\nSource of the figures: Makera's public Z1 page (https://global.makera.com/pages/makera-z1). No vendor post text is used.\n\n## Readings\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test makera_z1`: 4 passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test machine`: 61 passed.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `the_z1_models_are_listed_and_state_makeras_figures`: the Pro is listed, its 2000 mm/min ceilings, and its post name.\n- `a_default_op_on_the_z1_posts_m7_m9_through_the_carvera_post`: one M7 and one M9 for each model.\n- `travel_past_the_z1_refuses_by_name` and `a_tool_past_the_z1s_spindle_ceiling_refuses_by_name`: the refusals name each model.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No `cargo xtask gate quick` run. The author ran the two touched test binaries only.\n- No air cut on a Z1 Pro.\n- No post script changed, so the example catalog suites are not run.\n\nChangelog: Built-in machine Makera Z1 Pro (2000 mm/min), posted through the Carvera post.\n\nFixes #4434\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
